;; The module _socket (PY6e; Modules/socketmodule.c): BSD sockets over Go's syscall, for socket.py and what imports
;; it (doctest through pdb, subprocess's and asyncio's loopback pairs, test.support.socket_helper). A socket object
;; keeps its descriptor, family, type, protocol and timeout; a timeout is CPython's: the descriptor non-blocking and
;; each operation waiting on select(2) for at most the timeout (sock_call_ex). Addresses are CPython's tuples for
;; AF_INET and AF_INET6, a str or bytes path for AF_UNIX (a leading NUL: Linux's abstract namespace). Names resolve
;; as musl's getaddrinfo does through /etc/hosts and /etc/services (no DNS query: the tests run on loopback only).

